
>> title: Shepherd’s Pie
>> source: https://www.thewholesomedish.com/the-best-classic-shepherds-pie
>> servings: 6


== Make the Meat Filling ==

Add @olive oil{2%tbsp} to a large #skillet{} and place it over medium-high heat for ~{2%minutes}. Add @onion{1}(chopped). Cook for ~{5%minutes}, stirring occasionally.

Add @ground beef{1%lb}(90% lean) to the skillet and break it apart with a wooden spoon. Add @parsley{2%tsp}, @rosemary{1%tsp}, @thyme{1%tsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp}, and @ground black pepper{1/2%tsp}. Stir well. Cook for ~{6-8%minutes}, until the meat is browned, stirring occasionally.

Add @Worcestershire sauce{1%tbsp} and @garlic{2%cloves}(minced). Stir to combine. Cook for ~{1%minute}.

Add @flour{2%tbsp} and @tomato paste{2%tbsp}. Stir until well incorporated and no clumps of tomato paste remain.

Add @beef broth{1%cup}, @peas and carrots{1%cup}(frozen), and @corn kernels{1/2%cup}(frozen). Bring the liquid to a boil then reduce to simmer. Simmer for ~{5%minutes}, stirring occasionally.

Set the meat mixture aside. Preheat oven to 400 degrees F.

== Make the Potato Topping ==

Place @russet potatoes{1 1/2-2%lb}(about 2 large, peeled and cut into 1 inch cubes) in a large #pot{}. Cover the potatoes with water. Bring the water to a boil. Reduce to a simmer. Cook until potatoes are fork tender, ~{10-15%minutes}.

Drain the potatoes in a #colander{}. Return the potatoes to the hot pot. Let the potatoes rest in the hot pot for ~{1%minute} to evaporate any remaining liquid.

Add @butter{8%tbsp}(unsalted), @half & half{1/3%cup}, @garlic powder{1/2%tsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp}, and @ground black pepper{1/4%tsp}. Mash the potatoes and stir until all the ingredients are mixed together.

Add @parmesan cheese{1/4%cup} to the potatoes. Stir until well combined.

== Assemble the Casserole ==

Pour the meat mixture into a #9x9 inch baking dish{}. Spread it out into an even layer. Spoon the mashed potatoes on top of the meat. Carefully spread into an even layer.

If the baking dish looks very full, place it on a rimmed #baking sheet{} so that the filling doesn’t bubble over into your oven. Bake uncovered for ~{25-30%minutes}. Cool for ~{15%minutes} before serving.